{"id": "EUVD-2026-59638", "enisaUuid": "efd5554f-b5a1-308b-8aca-d0736f45496e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/arm-smmu-v3-iommufd: Require exactly one Stream ID for a vDEVICE\n\narm_vsmmu_vsid_to_sid() maps a guest's vSID to a single physical Stream ID\ntaken from master->streams[0], assuming a device has exactly one stream. A\ndevice with several streams gets only its first one mapped, so a guest vSID\ninvalidation cannot reach the others' ATC and IOTLB entries; a device with\nnone makes master->streams a ZERO_SIZE_PTR, read out of bounds.\n\nAdd an arm_vsmmu_vdevice_init() op to reject the vDEVICE with -EOPNOTSUPP\nwhen master->num_streams is not one, rather than mapping it silently.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:28:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:56", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3808bab5d95ae79e333e11f6a73d178e084c645d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0acbc621341aca4eb94d9c2f43e1ab273ff088f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3b8ee84a965058b41275069d4696f37a8b14bf6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74573", "GHSA-p5wj-hqvh-c7x4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f4b2892-4cf2-38f1-9861-29064527d3a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "24d58b29-2ec5-3de9-81df-f99080cc2c0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "489c2221-dffd-33e3-a6eb-583c57b2a631", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d68beb276ba26cec47350a6d468e967673ee0c56 <c3b8ee84a965058b41275069d4696f37a8b14bf6"}, {"id": "897b6505-e180-3c69-a219-583e621febd5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "8c160c44-c00e-32ec-9d10-6c8728273f87", "product": {"n